<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Jan-Oct trade gap rises to CZK 125.5 bln.</title>
<headline>Czech Jan-Oct trade gap rises to CZK 125.5 bln.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech trade balance for the first 10 months of 1996 rose to 125.5 billion crowns from a revised deficit of 109.6 billion for the January-September period, the Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The trade deficit for the January-October period in 1995 was 72.1 billion crowns.</p>
